1438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Ans: Bagging \(Bootstrap Aggregating\) trains models in parallel on random subsets of data and averages results to reduce variance. Boosting trains models sequentially, with each new model focusing on previous models' errors, reducing bias but potentially increasing variance.)
/E (Ans: Bagging \(Bootstrap Aggregating\) trains models in parallel on random subsets of data and averages results to reduce variance. Boosting trains models sequentially, with each new model focusing on previous models' errors, reducing bias but potentially increasing variance.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
